module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "declared_type_wall_keyed_on_the_value_being_a_kernel" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**the declared-type inhabitance wall decides on the KIND OF THE OFFENDING VALUE rather than on inhabitance, so it refuses a kernel literal at a declared type and admits a WRONG COPRODUCT ARM at the same position.** DESIGN section 4b puts `values inhabit declared types` in the ordinary compiler floor, so a breach is a below-baseline safety regression and not a rung on the ladder.",

    "READ FROM THE RELATION, NOT INFERRED FROM ITS NAME. `v1.compiler.infer` `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch_bounded` short-circuits at its second guard: `if is_kernel_type(name: actual_name) == false || actual_name == \"Unit\" { false }`. A `false` there is `no mismatch`, so an actual value whose authored name is not a kernel type leaves the relation before any formal type is consulted. Every position that consults this relation inherits that exit.",

    "WHY THIS IS NOT `one more declared-type position needs a member`, which is the natural reading and the wrong one. `test.claim.declared_type_kernel_inhabitance_witness_test` records that the census enumerated fourteen declared-type positions from the grammar -- every `parse_type_expr` call site in `v1.compiler.parse` -- and that seven admitted an `Int` where a coproduct was declared. Those seven were closed. But the guard above sits INSIDE the relation those positions now consult, so closing a position does nothing for a non-kernel wrong value: the record-literal field seam was ALREADY closed for kernels (that witness cites `KHold { subject: 5 }` refusing there) and still admits a wrong coproduct arm. The uncovered half is not a position, it is every position.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN ONE (2026-08-25, `gentle-eagle-360`, controlled fixture): with `AlphaRefusal` and `BetaRefusal` distinct coproducts and `Wrapper = WrapsBeta { cause: BetaRefusal }`, a fn returning `WrapsBeta { cause: c }` for `c: AlphaRefusal` is ACCEPTED, while the same field given an `Int` is refused and given an undeclared constructor is refused. The two refusals are what make the acceptance a measurement rather than an absence of checking.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN TWO (2026-09-10, gunbc#10952, found by review 63271): `data bmc_rotation_route_disposition: Disposition = SingleAuthority`, where `SingleAuthority` is an arm of `ConstructionMechanism` and `Disposition` declares only `Terminal` and `Scaffold`. It rode FOUR GREEN REQUIRED CHECKS. Two independent observations that it compiled rather than being skipped: a `gunbc run` over that closure resolved it and failed only on a wrong function name, and the pull request was green on all four required checks with the row present.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN THREE (2026-09-22, main ff2110b7e24, `quiet-ibex-229` from a `neat-boar-16` measurement, discovered by `loyal-swift-608` while demoting `lively-bat-737`'s construction wall): A COLLECTION AND A NOMINAL PRODUCT WERE MUTUALLY ADMITTED AT A DECLARED POSITION, IN BOTH DIRECTIONS. THE SIX-CELL GRID, each cell one `gunbc run --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --source-root <probe> --entry <probe>.dag --function probe` over a one-module fixture. ADMITTED, body ran and returned: `type Rec { a: String }` with `fn takes_rec(r: Rec)` given `fn a_list() -> List<String>`; and the dual, `fn takes_list(xs: List<Int>)` given `fn a_rec() -> Rec`. REFUSED, so the direct-call seam demonstrably runs on these fixtures: `Int <- String`, `Int <- List<Int>`, `Rec <- Other` (a second record), `Rec <- Optional<Int>`. The two admissions are therefore a hole in the relation, not an unreached position.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN THREE, re-derived per DESIGN section 6b rather than patched at the symptom. `v1.compiler.infer` `declared_type_inhabitance`, declared=`Rec`, produced=`List<String>`: the optional arm does not fire; declared is not generic; both names resolve; `declared_realizes_as_kernel_numeric` no; `collection_at_scalar_declared_type` REFUSES ONLY WHEN THE DECLARED BASE PEELS TO A KERNEL SCALAR and `Rec` does not, so false; `record_at_scalar_needs_identity` wants a kernel declared, no; `coproduct_at_record_declared_type` wants a coproduct produced, no; `refinement_inhabitance` Absent; `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch` false because the actual is not a kernel -- THE EXACT GUARD THIS ROW NAMES; `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required` no; `nominal_product_inhabitance_refusal` asks `nominal_product_head_name(produced)`, which answers the empty string for a collection BY DESIGN, so none. The relation then reaches its TERMINAL ARM, `Inhabits`, BY FALLTHROUGH. The dual falls through the same way with the roles swapped. THE EARLIEST UNJUSTIFIED BOUNDARY is that the relation's terminal arm is ACCEPTANCE while no arm ever judged collection-versus-nominal-product disjointness: every arm keys on the kind of ONE side, which is this row's recognition rule seen in a second vocabulary -- `is_kernel_type` on the actual is one instance of it and `node_is_collection` on the produced is another.",

    "WHAT SPECIMEN THREE'S REPAIR IS, AND WHAT IT IS NOT. gunbc#12045 replaces `collection_at_scalar_declared_type` with `collection_versus_established_identity`, a RELATION BETWEEN THE TWO SIDES: exactly one side is an element or keyed collection after `peel_nominal_alias_identity` on BOTH sides, and the other side is an ESTABLISHED non-generic identity -- kernel scalar, nominal product or coproduct by `expected_type_head_exposure`. It is a replacement rather than a sibling arm precisely because a second relation keyed on products is the fork this row exists to prevent. THAT IS STILL NOT THIS ROW'S NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER. The trigger names ONE JUDGMENT FROM THE FORMAL'S DECLARATION FOR AN ACTUAL OF ANY KIND, sufficient for removing the offending-value guards entirely; the repair removes one such guard and leaves `kernel_value_declared_type_mismatch` and the head-name arms standing. The row stays open, and a future change may retire it only by landing exactly the trigger.",

    "HARM, AND IT IS THE SECOND SPECIMEN THAT SHOWS THE SHAPE. The review that found it concluded `the module therefore does not compile, and with it the whole witness closure` -- reasonable, and false. So the defect does not merely admit a wrong value: it makes a reader who assumes the floor holds derive a WRONG CONSEQUENCE from a correct observation. The author had four green checks saying the row was fine and a reviewer saying the module was absent, and neither was true.",

    "DISTINGUISHING FACTS: this is NOT the evidence-overreach family (a receipt supporting more than its instrument established) -- nothing here is a receipt, and the claim is not about coverage. It is NOT `check_subject_shape_cannot_represent_the_state_the_check_detects` -- the relation can represent the state perfectly; it declines to look. The tell is a wall whose guard names a property of the OFFENDING VALUE (`is_kernel_type`) where the property under test is a RELATION between the value and its declared type.",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: below the floor, which is not a rung. The class is decidable and the authority exists -- `lookup_type_by_name` and the declared-type env are already in hand at the guard that exits -- so this is DESIGN section 5's `wall after grounding` with the grounding already present. CEILING: structurally guaranteed; a wrong-typed literal is authorable in source, so impossibility is not available, but no `Accepted` program need contain one. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, NAMED AS A CAPABILITY: an inhabitance judgment that decides from the FORMAL type's declaration for an actual value of ANY kind -- kernel, coproduct arm, record literal, alias -- SUFFICIENT FOR removing `is_kernel_type` from the guard entirely rather than adding a second relation beside it. A second relation keyed on coproducts would be the fork this row exists to prevent.",

    "MEASURED SPECIMEN FOUR (2026-09-24, reported by lane `bold-raven-671` against a private specimen, reproduced by `keen-stag-684` on public main cfb9ff8): a NULLARY FOREIGN ARM at the data-initializer and declared-return positions. Fixture: `type FvAlpha = FvX | FvY`, `type FvBeta = FvZ | FvW`, `data fv_v: FvBeta = FvX`, `fn fv_ret() -> FvBeta { FvX }`. INTERPRETER (`gunbc run`): a fn declared `-> FvBeta` returning `fv_v` evaluated to an FvAlpha, and a total match over FvBeta's two arms died with `PatternMatchFailure { value: \"FvX\" }`. EMIT ROUTE (`gunbc compile --target rust`): `compiled: 6 files emitted, 0 diagnostics`, emitting `pub fn fv_ret() -> FvBeta { FvAlpha::FvX }` -- the refusal deferred to rustc, which is outside the modeled guarantee.",

    "THE CHAIN FOR SPECIMEN FOUR, per DESIGN section 6b. The bare arm's inferred type is correct: `variant_reference_inferred_node` keeps the owner the binder chose (FvAlpha) because the expected FvBeta does not own FvX, so the reference link is justified. Both positions then reach `declared_type_conformance_diags`, which judged ground kernels, ground element collections, nominal products and callables, and had NO ARM for a coproduct pair -- while `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required`, the relation the record-literal field seam and `declared_type_inhabitance` already consult for exactly this pair, sat unconsulted there. That seam is the earliest unjustified boundary for these two positions. REPAIR: `declared_type_conformance_diags` consumes `coproduct_payload_where_parent_required` -- the existing relation at two more positions, no new relation. RED and positive control: `test.claim.declared_type_foreign_variant_witness_test` (a foreign arm refused at both positions; the native arm accepted at both), in the required gate by the `test.claim.declared_type_` prefix; the two refusing members return false on the pre-change binary and true after.",

    "SPECIMEN FOUR'S BLAST RADIUS, ENUMERATED BY IDENTITY AND FIXED FORWARD, NOT EXEMPTED. The instrument is a differential of the whole-corpus covering compile (`gunbc compile --source-root dag --source-root src/v2 --target rust --repository gunbc --measured-root-demands tools/whole_corpus_compile_measured_root_demands.json`) run with the pre-repair and post-repair binaries: the sorted blocking `error[..]` lines of each, compared, name every newly refused site by file and position. On main cfb9ff8 the repair newly refused 67 sites in two groups. GROUP ONE, SPECIMEN TWO'S SHAPE (63): `data <name>: Disposition = SingleAuthority` rows in production modules, the planted nullary fixture `test.fixture.decl_facts_reflection.specimens` `planted_nullary_disposition_specimen` of the same shape, and that module's `mechanism_data_ref`, declared `ConstructionMechanism` but initialised with the Disposition arm `Terminal`. Fixed forward by retyping each SingleAuthority row's annotation to the type its value inhabits (`ConstructionMechanism`) and by initialising `mechanism_data_ref` with `RealizationDispatch`; the production rows have no consumer outside their own files, and the two fixture rows keep the shape their witnesses assert (a top-level nullary arm named SingleAuthority; a coproduct-typed data reference that is not a variant value). Specimen two was therefore not one row but a population that four green checks never saw. GROUP TWO, PAYLOAD WHERE PARENT REQUIRED (4): functions declared `-> ContentHash` whose body returns the bare `Fnv1a64Structural` payload of `content_hash_atom` -- `v2.compiler.emit_host` `emit_host_string_list_digest`, `test.claim.roadmap_static_site_witness` `fixture_site_artifact_digest`, `gunbc.host_identity_adopt` `host_identity_adopt_model_hash`, `gunbc.host_identity_assimilation` `host_identity_assimilation_model_hash`. Fixed forward at the consumer's declared type: the first two feed `Fnv1a64Structural` fields (`std.artifact_store` `ArtifactRealizationInput.content_digest`, the roadmap artifact `digest`), so their returns are retyped; the last two feed `ContentHash` `model_hash` fields, so their values are wrapped with `std.content_hash` `as_content_hash_structural`. After both groups the post-repair blocking set equals the pre-repair set line for line.",

    "WHAT SPECIMEN FOUR'S REPAIR IS NOT: this row's trigger. It adds a consumer of an existing arm at two positions; it does not remove `is_kernel_type` from any guard, and the relation it consumes still excludes GENERIC coproducts and compares arm NAME SETS rather than declaration identity. The positional next step is wiring `PositionDataInitializer` and `PositionDeclaredReturn` as `DeclaredTypeObligation` producers into `declared_type_obligation_diags`, so these positions consult the ONE relation rather than a hand-picked arm of it; the row's capability trigger stands unchanged.",

    "NOT CLAIMED HERE: how many of the fourteen positions admit a wrong coproduct. The guard's placement implies all of them, and I did not measure them one at a time. A census across the fourteen positions with a non-kernel wrong value is the honest next measurement, and it is probably worth more than any single new witness member.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
